From: Balázs Gyimesi <gyimesi.balazs@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] nss_rmnet_rx: let paged frags through, leave GRO segments to the stack

The bind handler linearized every non-linear packet before framing it. A
frag list has to be flattened, since the firmware cannot hand it back, but
paged frags are what a zero-copy rmnet deaggregation produces and what
nss_core_send_buffer() already sends as a scatter-gather chain; linearize
only the former.

A device that delivers through GRO (rmnet) also hands the handler merged
segments. The firmware returns one it does not accelerate as a single
packet whose checksum state is gone, and TCP then verifies a checksum over
the merged payload and drops it: TcpInCsumErrors on every host-bound flow
through a QMAP link. Leave merged segments to the stack; a flow that is
accelerated never comes back this way.

Injected packets are also offered to the firmware for reuse as its empty
buffers (module parameter rmnet_reusable), so that one it accepts is not
returned, freed and replaced by a fresh allocation per packet. The firmware
holds them for the duration of a burst; above rmnet_reuse_max held buffers
no more are offered.
--- a/nss_rmnet_rx.c
+++ b/nss_rmnet_rx.c
@@ -22,6 +22,25 @@
  */
 
 #include "nss_tx_rx_common.h"
+
+/*
+ * Let the firmware keep an injected packet's buffer as one of its empty
+ * buffers instead of returning it (nss_core_skb_can_reuse() decides whether
+ * a buffer qualifies).
+ */
+static bool nss_rmnet_rx_reusable = true;
+module_param_named(rmnet_reusable, nss_rmnet_rx_reusable, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(rmnet_reusable, "offer injected rmnet buffers to the firmware for reuse");
+
+/*
+ * The firmware holds the buffers it accepts for the duration of a burst and
+ * hands them back when the traffic stops (measured: ~13k buffers idle, ~23k
+ * during a download, back to 13k within a minute). Stop offering buffers
+ * above this many held, so that a long burst cannot grow the set unbounded.
+ */
+static unsigned int nss_rmnet_rx_reuse_max = 20480;
+module_param_named(rmnet_reuse_max, nss_rmnet_rx_reuse_max, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(rmnet_reuse_max, "offer no buffer for reuse while the firmware holds more than this many");
 #include "nss_rmnet_rx_stats.h"
 #include <net/arp.h>
 #include <linux/netfilter.h>
@@ -554,6 +573,7 @@
 {
 	int32_t if_num = handle->if_num_h2n;
 	struct nss_ctx_instance *nss_ctx = handle->nss_ctx;
+	uint32_t flag;
 	int cpu = 0;
 
 	if (unlikely(nss_ctl_redirect == 0)) {
@@ -586,7 +606,13 @@
 	put_cpu();
 	skb_set_queue_mapping(skb, cpu);
 
-	return nss_core_send_packet(nss_ctx, skb, if_num, H2N_BIT_FLAG_VIRTUAL_BUFFER);
+	flag = H2N_BIT_FLAG_VIRTUAL_BUFFER;
+	if (nss_rmnet_rx_reusable &&
+	    NSS_PKT_STATS_READ(&nss_ctx->nss_top->stats_drv[NSS_DRV_STATS_NSS_SKB_COUNT]) < nss_rmnet_rx_reuse_max) {
+		flag |= H2N_BIT_FLAG_BUFFER_REUSABLE;
+	}
+
+	return nss_core_send_packet(nss_ctx, skb, if_num, flag);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(nss_rmnet_rx_tx_buf);
 
@@ -972,7 +998,22 @@
 	 * zero: the source interface comes from the node pair and any
 	 * forwarding decision from the rule.
 	 */
-	if (skb_is_nonlinear(skb) && skb_linearize(skb)) {
+	/*
+	 * A segment GRO merged: the firmware would return it as one packet
+	 * without its checksum state, and TCP would verify the checksum over
+	 * the merged payload. The stack handles it; an accelerated flow never
+	 * comes back this way.
+	 */
+	if (skb_is_gso(skb)) {
+		return RX_HANDLER_PASS;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * A frag list the firmware could not hand back, so it is flattened;
+	 * paged frags go down as a scatter-gather chain when the device
+	 * advertises SG, and nss_core linearizes them otherwise.
+	 */
+	if (skb_has_frag_list(skb) && skb_linearize(skb)) {
 		return RX_HANDLER_PASS;
 	}
 
